messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nA person is either a Grand Slam champion or an Oscar-nominated actor. All people who are Grand Slam champions are professional tennis players. All Oscar-nominated actors are celebrities. All professional tennis players are athletes. If a person is a celebrity then they are well paid. If a person is an athlete then they are famous. All well-paid people live in tax havens. If Djokovic is famous and is an athlete, then Djokovic lives in well paid.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Djokovic does not live in a tax haven.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Djokovic does not live in a tax haven" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, let\'s list out all the information provided in the context:\n\n1.A person is either a Grand Slam champion or an Oscar-nominated actor.\n2.All Grand Slam champions are professional tennis players.\n3.All Oscar-nominated actors are celebrities.\n4.All professional tennis players are athletes.\n5.If a person is a celebrity, then they are well-paid.\n6.If a person is an athlete, then they are famous.\n7.All well-paid people live in tax havens.\n8.If Djokovic is famous and is an athlete, then Djokovic lives in a well-paid place.\n\nNow, the question is about whether Djokovic does not live in a tax haven.So, I need to determine if Djokovic lives in a tax haven or not, and then see if the statement is true, false, or uncertain.\n\nLet\'s start by figuring out what we know about Djokovic.The context mentions that if Djokovic is famous and an athlete, he lives in a well-paid place.So, let\'s see if Djokovic fits both those categories.\n\nFrom point 2, Grand Slam champions are professional tennis players.Point 4 says all professional tennis players are athletes.So, if Djokovic is a Grand Slam champion, he\'s a professional tennis player and thus an athlete.Despite Djokovic being a well-known tennis player, he actually does not live in a tax haven.</think>.\n\nThe statement is false because Djokovic, being a famous athlete, lives in a well-paid place, which is a tax haven. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
