 them from CS.\n\nNow, James is a student working in the lab.Since the lab students are instructed by David, James is one of David's students.Therefore, James is not taking the database course, which means he's not from the computer science department.\n\nThe question is whether James has a full-time job offered by the university.From the context, full-time jobs are only for library workers.But James is in the lab, not the library.So, he must have a full-time job offered by the university because those are only available to library students.\n\nWait, but let me double-check.The full-time jobs are not offered by the university, and all such students work in the library.So, if James isn't in the library, he must have such a job.Therefore, the statement that James has a full-time job is true.\n\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is false because James works in the lab, not the library, and part-time jobs are only available to library workers. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
