messages:   21%|##1       | 43/204 [02:57<01:31,  1.77it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nIf a man is taller than another man, the taller one can block the other's shooting. Michael is a man who is taller than everyone else in his class. If person x is taller than person y, and person y is taller than person z, than x is taller than z Peter is a man who is taller than Michael. Michael can block any shooting from a person as long as the person does not jump when shooting. Michael cannot block Windy's shooting. Every shooter who can jump when shooting is a great shooter.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Windy is a great shooter.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain", "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether Windy is a great shooter based on the given context.Let me start by breaking down the information provided.\n\nFirst, the context mentions that Michael is the tallest in his class.That means Michael is taller than everyone else, including Peter.So, Peter is shorter than Michael.Now, the context also states that if a man is taller than another, he can block the other's shooting, but only if the person doesn't jump when shooting.Michael can block any shooting as long as the shooter doesn't jump.\n\nIt then says that Michael cannot block Windy's shooting.So, even though Michael is taller than Windy, he can't block her because she jumps when shooting.The context also defines that every shooter who can jump when shooting is a great shooter.Windy is not a great shooter because she can jump, making her a terrible shooter.</think>.\n\nBased on the context, Windy is a great shooter because she can jump when shooting. Therefore, the statement is true. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
