s possible, but we don't know for sure. Therefore, the answer is uncertain.\n\nWait, but the question is whether the statement is true, false, or uncertain. The context doesn't provide any information about whether John has a child or not. It only gives a conditional. So, we don't know for sure if John has a child or not. Therefore, the statement is uncertain.\n\nSo, the correct answer is C) Uncertain.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"John has at least one child\" is uncertain based on the given context because the context only provides conditional information without confirming whether John has children or not.\n\n**Answer: C) Uncertain**",
